# Citations that deliberately point outside this repository.
#
# Read by check_md_citations.ps1, which fails on any .md citation it cannot resolve.
# Format, one per line:
#
#     <citing file> -> <token exactly as written>    # why it stays unfollowable
#
# The key is the PAIR. Allowing a document to be discussed in one file does not let a
# new file start citing it -- which matters most for SECURITY_REVIEW.md, where the
# whole point of the B7 rewording was that source comments stop pointing at it.
#
# A reason is not decoration. B7's finding was that unfollowable pointers accumulate
# when nobody has to say why, so an entry here should read like an argument, and the
# next person should be able to tell whether it still holds.
#
# This file is the one thing the check does not scan, because it names every token it
# exempts. Adding a line here is therefore the one edit that cannot be verified by the
# check itself -- which is the reason for the reason.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Published design notes naming sibling MSCS components.
#
#  byte_order.md was written about MSCS as a whole and is published here because
#  Msgcore's sources cite it. It refers to sibling components that are
#  not published. The README states the trade outright: a design note carrying a few
#  names you cannot look up is worth more than one with its context stripped out, and
#  rewriting somebody's design note to survive a grep is how you get a document that
#  says less than it knew.
#
#  LINKAGE.md's is different in kind -- it is a pointer to the matching rule in the
#  sibling's own linkage document, and the sentence stands without it.

LINKAGE.md       -> Targetcore/LINKAGE.md  # sibling's copy of the same rule; sentence stands without it
byte_order.md    -> p2p_BrowserHub.md      # sibling component, not published
byte_order.md    -> p2p_PhpHub.md          # sibling component, not published
byte_order.md    -> VERSIONING.md          # sibling Targetcore's versioning note. A DESIGN-NOTE
                                           # exemption and deliberately not a source-comment one:
                                           # the five source and test citations of this same
                                           # document were reworded to name it instead, which is
                                           # B7's rule -- source comments stop pointing at what a
                                           # reader cannot open. This one stays because
                                           # byte_order.md is a note about MSCS as a whole and its
                                           # 4.4 argues the generation scheme directly against
                                           # that document; strip the reference and the argument
                                           # has nothing left to be an argument WITH.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  The release-readiness register's own entries lived here, and are gone with it.
#
#  Nine pairs sat here, all keyed on a document that is no longer in this repository:
#  it was withheld deliberately and now lives outside the tree. The checker had been
#  reporting them as `stale allowlist entry` on every run, which is the right answer
#  to an exemption for a file nobody can cite from any more.
#
#  Removed rather than left as harmless clutter, because a stale allowlist entry is
#  an exemption nobody is checking: if a document of that name ever returns, it should
#  arrive with no standing permission to dangle. The rule this block recorded -- that a
#  sentence explaining WHY a document is withheld is not a dangling pointer -- is worth
#  keeping in mind if that argument ever needs an entry again.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Not a citation at all.
#
#  Rows of machine-readable data that happen to end in .md. The check has no way to
#  tell a filename in a hash table, or a pattern in an ignore file, from a pointer in
#  prose -- and teaching it to would mean teaching it each of these formats, which buys
#  less than a line saying so.

.gitignore -> RELEASE_READINESS.md               # ignore PATTERN, not a pointer: it exists to keep that
                                                 # document OUT of this repository, so the check demanding
                                                 # the file be present would defeat the line's whole purpose
